 "verdict": "RUNG: 9 of 9 cells from selection_mode.json measured; ids and s_far are READ from it rather than recomputed, so this cannot disagree with F123 by construction.  PRIMARY: rho(H_gap, s_far) = +0.567 on the settled pool and +0.783 on the uniform pool, n = 9 each. At or above the registered 0.6 threshold, so how much the FAR token reduces uncertainty is a strong correlate of how much it propagates damage -- the mechanism F123 left open now has a named candidate. SECONDARY: rho(H_cond, s_far) = +0.367 settled, +0.333 uniform -- whether the alphabet is merely FLAT rather than informative about the far token. BOUNDARY: same model (EleutherAI/pythia-410m step4000), T = 0.7, r = 2 and geometry as F123. n = 9 cells, so only a large effect is visible, and naming a correlate is not naming a cause.",
